  "question": {
    "text": "A light ray is incident on the lower medium boundary at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with the normal. Which of the following statements is true?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0103_8c7e2a12213b.jpg\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 131px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "If <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&gt;</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;,then total deviation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "If <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#956;</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&#60;</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;, then total deviation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "If <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#956;</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&#62;</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;,then total deviation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "If <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#956;</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&#60;</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;,then total deviation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; T.I.R. at A<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mo>sin</mo> <mn>3</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>sin</mo> <mn>9</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><strong>Case -I</strong><br /><br />If <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&lt;</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>, then always T.I.R. takes place and in this situation angle of deviation is 120<sup>o</sup>.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0103_0c2cde3ea07f.jpg\" style=\"width: 190px; height: 149px;\" /><br /><br /><strong>Case-II</strong><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&gt;</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>, then for the given angle of incidence no. T.I.R takes place at A, so light strikes on interface B for T.I.R.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0103_491e56b75765.jpg\" style=\"width: 206px; height: 180px;\" /><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>sin</mo> <mi>α</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>sin</mo> <mn>9</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mo>sin</mo> <mi>α</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>sin</mo> <mi>α</mi> <mo>&lt;</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&gt;</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>"
  }
}